        <mxCell id="c149" value="&lt;i&gt;Report view, page Credits Cycle of Audit Monitoring, in a different arrangement from the model answer&#x27;s (its text box with the written answer is not drawn). The matrix gives, for each new test, the exceptions, the population and the rate per 1,000 by year and over the three years; the Total row&#x27;s population and rate are blank (outlined in coral) because the Population measure reads one process at a time. The cards count the register: 992 exceptions, of which 15 are reviewed, 841 covered by a design finding (outlined in teal, as in the table) and 136 open, as before the four tests; the table&#x27;s Open Exceptions is blank because every exception of the new tests is covered. In amber, the date each finding covers through (12/31/2026) and the date it is to be fixed (12/31/2027): exceptions dated later stay open for review.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="528" width="860" height="98" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
